# .bbignore — what this repository does NOT index.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore (bb reads it through the `ignore` package, alongside
# .gitignore, before any parsing). Lines are additive exclusions; nothing here
# changes what bb indexes for any OTHER project.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (measured 2026-10-08) ──────────────────────────────
#
# `bb index .` on this checkout discovered 11,045 files and ~944k symbols, and
# the run was dominated by its own generated artefacts rather than by source.
# Evidence from the run's own log:
#
#   [STORE] elixir-grammar-ab.json:            10103 symbols
#   [STORE] incoming-audit-1875files.json:      8753 symbols
#   [STORE] zig-absent-class-3848.json:         2153 symbols
#   [STORE] elixir-grammar-ab.json ...  ...  (validation/m60/results, m12/ground-truth,
#   [STORE] oracle-callsite-scoped-cpp-f30.json: 678   m13/results, m59/results, ...)
#
# and the parent indexer spent 31 of one run's 34 minutes with its event loop
# BLOCKED (single blocks of 15s, 89s, 250s) storing them. JSON was 3,514 files /
# 816,369 symbols — 86% of everything indexed. These are outputs of this
# programme's own gates: `.gitignore` already states the rule for them
# ("Generated M60 census/oracle output — NEVER in git (programme rule 7)"). An
# index of this repository should be an index of the repository's CODE.
#
# Nothing here is deleted or hidden from git: every excluded path stays tracked,
# reviewable and gated. `bb index` simply stops reading generated evidence as if
# it were source. Delete a line to put that tree back in the index.

# ── Programme evidence output (rule 7) ──────────────────────────────────────
validation/**/results/
validation/**/measurements/
validation/**/ground-truth/
validation/**/oracle-shapes/
validation/**/patches/
validation/**/tmp/
validation/**/unversioned-recovered/
validation/m60/**/*.json
validation/m60/**/*.log

# Raw walk/row dumps and logs are data, not source (and are gitignored anyway).
**/*.ndjson

# ── Worktree snapshots: whole copies of src/ at old revisions ───────────────
# 286 tracked files, including FOUR divergent copies of script/m14/differential.ts
# (14,140 / 14,355 / 14,355 / 17,581 lines). Indexing them stores duplicate
# symbols for the same analyse(s) and pollutes every later search.
worktree-snapshots/

# ── Vendored tree-sitter grammar artefacts ──────────────────────────────────
# 351 files / 72 MB of GENERATED grammar tables (node-types.json up to 514 KB,
# grammar.json up to 429 KB) and the parsers built from them. Measured in the
# run: `[STORE] node-types.json: 3369 symbols`, `[STORE] grammar.json: 1635` —
# one grammar table costs more to store than the whole analyzer lane that
# consumes it, and none of it is this project's code.
grammars/

# ── The fixture corpus (the last 20% that costs as much as the first 80%) ───
# 3,936 files / 207 MB — 44% of everything discovered — of which 1,483 are
# `*.expectation.json` plus a fixture source in each of the 46 lanes. They are
# the programme's ground truth and they stay tracked, reviewed and gated; but
# `analysis-exclusions.ts` ALREADY hides every `fixtures` directory from analysis
# results, so indexing them stores symbols that no analysis surface will show.
#
# Measured: the 40%->95% stretch of a run (7m7s -> 26m12s) is almost entirely
# this tree. Excluding it is what makes an index of this repository an index of
# its CODE.
#
# To walk the fixture corpus itself, run bb with validation/m14/fixtures as the
# project root — that is a different question, and it gets its own database:
#   bb index validation/m14/fixtures
validation/**/fixtures/

# ── Scratch probe trees: method, not product ────────────────────────────────
# Keep them on disk and in git (they are the method behind shipped numbers);
# they are not part of the code graph.
.tmp-probe/

# ── Absolute-precision exclusions of the biggest single offenders ───────────
# Named so a reader can see exactly which file motivated the rule above.
validation/m60/grammar-survey.json
validation/m60/grammar-survey.cache.json
validation/m60/target-spelling-register.json
validation/m60/script-surface-baseline.json
validation/m49/regex-debt-register.json
validation/m12/ground-truth/

# ── Local measurement databases and scratch roots ───────────────────────────
# Found by auditing the index against `git ls-files`: three files —
# `.bb-bench/status`, `.bb-prof/status`, `.bb-scope/status` — were indexed out of
# throwaway databases created for the index-speed measurements, because nothing
# excluded them and bb honours only .gitignore/.bbignore. They are regenerable
# data, never source, and their rows then outlive the directories they came from
# (freshness reported them missing until the next run purged them).
.bb-*/

